CHAPTER III
OBLIGATIONS AND RESPONSIBILITIES
Article 4
(1) The Regional Government has the obligation and responsibility to implement efforts to prevent the occurrence of violence in the form of:
a. providing data and information about gender and child victims of violence in accordance with laws and regulations;
b. conducting education on anti-violence values based on gender and violence against children; and
c. disseminating laws and regulations related to the implementation of protection against gender-based violence and child victims of violence.
(2) To anticipate the occurrence of acts of violence, the Regional Government has the obligation to provide and organize services for victims in the form of:
a. establishing and facilitating the operation of integrated service institutions for victims by involving elements of SKPD, Agencies, Institutions, Community Organizations, the Community;
b. providing facilities and infrastructure;
c. increasing the capacity of service provider institutions;
d. conducting coordination and cooperation in the implementation of protection for victims of gender-based violence and child victims of violence;
e. conducting monitoring and evaluation.
f. encouraging public awareness of the importance of protection for victims.
(3) The Regional Government in carrying out obligations as referred to in paragraph (1) and (2) must pay attention to the rights and obligations of parents, guardians, husbands or other persons who are legally responsible for the victim.

Article 20
The field of repatriation and social reintegration as referred to in Article 15 paragraph (2) letter e has the following duties:
a. coordinating and facilitating the repatriation process of victims and/or facilitating repatriation referrals to the Provincial PPT;
b. facilitating the reintegration process of victims of violence to their families, guardians, substitute families, communities, educational institutions or social institutions;
c. preparing progress reports on the repatriation assistance and social rehabilitation process; and
d. conducting monitoring for at least three months after the victim is returned to their family, guardian, substitute family, community.

CHAPTER X
COMMUNITY PARTICIPATION
Article 25
(1) The community participates in the implementation of protection for victims.
(2) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be in the form of:
a. providing protection for victims;
b. providing emergency assistance;
c. providing advocacy to victims and or the community regarding the handling of gender-based and child violence cases;
d. assisting in the process of submitting applications for protection orders;
e. conveying information to the authorized authorities related to cases of gender-based and child violence;
f. organizing the strengthening of community groups in handling gender-based and child violence; and
g. disseminating information about laws and regulations related to gender-based and child violence.

CHAPTER II
PRINCIPLES AND OBJECTIVES
Article 2
The protection of victims of gender-based violence and children is based on Pancasila and grounded in the 1945 Constitution, as well as basic principles that include:
a. non-discrimination;
b. best interests of the victim;
c. gender justice and equality;
d. victim protection;
e. maternal survival;
f. child survival, growth, and development;
g. respect for the child's opinion;
h. transparency;
i. integration;
j. not blaming the victim;
k. empowering;
l. victim confidentiality;
m. decision-making in the hands of the victim.

REGENT OF PEKALONGAN,

Considering : a. that every citizen has the right to be free from torture or treatment that degrades human dignity, worth and honor and has the right to obtain security and freedom from all forms of violence and discrimination as a form of respect, protection and enforcement of Human Rights, particularly the basic rights of women and children, so it is necessary to regulate the implementation of protection for victims of gender-based violence and children in Pekalongan Regency;
b. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation of Pekalongan Regency concerning the Implementation of Protection for Victims of Gender-Based Violence and Children;

In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
